  "body": "For every occurrence of a match of the \"name\" attribute of a meta element, add the clarification that it should be a ASCII case-insensitive match. There was some inconsistency in how the \"name\" attribute value was used (`value set to`, `whose value is`, `attribute's value`), so I tried to insert the text in the most natural sounding way.\n\nFixes #3332\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3556/semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 15, 2018, 10:15 AM GMT (d9d4f5a)\">/semantics.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3556/d661e87...d9d4f5a/semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 15, 2018, 10:15 AM GMT (d9d4f5a)\">diff</a> )",
